dwg2pdf 0.5.1 / GUI 0.2.20 -- COMPLETE release, 2026-09-18
================================================================

Everything needed to run, test and rebuild. Nothing omitted.

  dwg2pdf.py                 engine, revision 0.5.1
  dwg2pdf_gui.py             Qt GUI (qt.py -> PySide6), revision 0.2.20
  test_autocad.py            181 checks, runs anywhere
  test_gui.py                 79 checks, needs a Qt platform
  test_images.py              23 checks
  make_test_drawings.py      generates test_drawings/ and test_images/
  README.md                  the whole record, including section 9
  environment-dwg2pdf.yml    mamba/conda environment
  build_libredwg.sh          rebuilds the bundled decoder from source
  vendor/libredwg-win64/     LibreDWG 0.14.8593, Windows x86-64
  dwg_samples/               real DWGs, five source versions
  docs/                      screenshots referenced by the README

0.5.1 FIXES A REGRESSION 0.5.0 SHIPPED -- READ THIS
---------------------------------------------------
0.5.0 changed --layouts to default to 'auto'. That was WRONG for a set
whose sheets draw in model space with a title block in paper space:

    0.4.x --layouts model : ... View Z-Z.dwg -> 94.5 KiB
    0.5.0 --layouts auto  : ... View Z-Z.dwg ->  1.5 KiB   (blank)

'auto' took any paperspace layout with a drawable entity in it, so it
chose the title block and discarded the drawing. In 0.5.1:
  * the default is 'model' again;
  * 'auto' WEIGHS the two spaces -- paperspace wins only when it
    carries at least as much as model space (AUTO_PAPER_SHARE).
Also gone: the 'invalid escape sequence' SyntaxWarning that printed
once per worker. Both modules now compile under -W error::SyntaxWarning
as part of the suite.

STILL FROM 0.5.0 (all good)
---------------------------
  * accoreconsole ANSWERS THE PROMPTS AutoCAD actually asks. The old
    fixed .scr assumed an order; 'Enter paper units' appears for some
    devices and not others, and one missing prompt shifted everything.
    The plot device was never the problem. --accore-mode script reverts.
  * acad-com no longer attaches to a RUNNING AutoCAD (--acad-attach
    opts back in), and recycles its own every 50 drawings.
  * the plot goes STRAIGHT TO THE DELIVERABLE -- the 0.4.0 scratch
    rename made the viewer report a missing file once per sheet.

INSTALL
-------
Unpack so that dwg2pdf.py and vendor/ are SIBLINGS. Verify:

    python dwg2pdf.py --probe

    LibreDWG dwg2dxf 0.14.8593 at ...\vendor\libredwg-win64\dwg2dxf.exe [bundled]

TEST
----
    python test_autocad.py        # 181, no AutoCAD needed
    python test_gui.py            #  79
    python test_images.py         #  23

Fixtures are generated on first run.

